    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for May 30th is headlined by two high-efficiency starts: **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Daulton Varsho** (72.31). **Bryson Stott** draws a favorable matchup against Roki Sasaki, benefiting from an impressive 19% boost due to the starter's poor xERA (5.11) and a strong platoon advantage that projects him for high-impact production in the #5 hole. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** is a top-tier play against Young; the combination of a favorable hitter's park and a weak opposing arm elevates his baseline, making him a cornerstone of today's production. **Tyler Freeman** (71.80) and **Matt Chapman** (70.21) also remain must-starts, as both leverage the favorable matchup against Feltner\u2014a pitcher whose profile aligns perfectly with our need for offensive volume in today's 5x5 setup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Gavin Sheets** (45.42), who remained the primary alternative to our active roster. While **Gavin Sheets** offers respectable power, he was ultimately sidelined by the superior efficiency scores of **Lawrence Butler** and **Jeremiah Jackson**, despite their own challenging matchups. We are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Will Smith**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Lawrence Butler**; should these projections fluctuate upon official release, our efficiency floor may shift. Furthermore, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (56.84) faces a stiff test against Sonny Gray; while his base projection is high, his score is tempered by a negative BvP history and a tougher pitching matchup, making him a player to watch closely as the game progresses. We are keeping **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Masyn Winn** on standby, as their efficiency scores hovered just above the 40-point threshold, serving as our primary insurance should any late-hour lineup adjustments occur.",
